{"prompt": {"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a helpful assistant that translates C++ code to Python 3 code. The code should reads and writes I/O from the console."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Translate the following GNU C++ code to Python 3 code. The code reads and writes I/O from the console. Your translated code should have the exact same functionality as the given code, meaning that it should have the same output for any given input.\nPrint your translated code and also the confidence score you give to your translation. The confidence score should be a number between 0 and 1. The format of the output should be:\n<translated_code>\n<your_translated_code>\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n<your_confidence_score>\n</confidence>\nDo not provide any other text or markdown fences.\n\nHere is the original GNU C++ code you have to translate:\n<original_code>\n#include<bits/stdc++.h>\nusing namespace std;\n#define mod 1000000007\ntypedef unsigned long long int LL;\nstruct M{\n    LL s[35][35],n;\n    friend M operator * (M a,M b){\n        M c;\n        c.n=a.n;\n        int i,j,k;\n        for(i=0;i<a.n;i++){\n            for(j=0;j<a.n;j++){\n                c.s[i][j]=0;\n                for(k=0;k<a.n;k++){\n                    c.s[i][j]+=a.s[i][k]*b.s[k][j];\n                    c.s[i][j]%=mod;\n                }\n            }\n        }\n        return c;\n    }\n}bi[65][65],I;\nint main(){\n    LL n,m,t,x,y,z,add;\n    int i,j,k;\n    scanf(\"%llu%llu\",&n,&m);\n    bi[0][0].n=m+1;\n    for(i=0;i<=m;i++){\n        bi[0][0].s[i][i]=1;\n        bi[0][0].s[0][i]=1;\n    }\n    x=0,y=1,z=0,add=0;\n    while(y*m<=n){\n        y*=m;\n        x++;\n    }\n    for(t=0;t<=x;t++){\n        if(t){\n            bi[t][0]=bi[t-1][0];\n            for(i=1;i<m;i++){\n                bi[t][0]=bi[t][0]*bi[t-1][i];\n            }\n        }\n        for(i=1;i<m;i++){\n            bi[t][i]=bi[t][i-1];\n            for(j=m-2;j>=0;j--){\n                for(k=0;k<=m;k++){\n                    swap(bi[t][i].s[j][k],bi[t][i].s[j+1][k]);\n                }\n            }\n            for(j=m-2;j>=0;j--){\n                for(k=0;k<=m;k++){\n                    swap(bi[t][i].s[k][j],bi[t][i].s[k][j+1]);\n                }\n            }\n        }\n\n    }\n    for(i=0;i<=m;i++){\n        I.n=m+1;\n        I.s[i][i]=1;\n    }\n    while(add<n){\n        //printf(\"%llu\",add);\n        if(add<=n-y){\n            add+=y;\n            I=I*bi[x][z];\n            z=(z+1)%m;\n        }\n        else{\n            y/=m;\n            x--;\n        }\n    }\n    //I.pt();\n    LL ans=0;\n    for(i=0;i<=m;i++){\n        ans=(ans+I.s[i][m])%mod;\n    }\n    printf(\"%llu\\n\",ans);\n}\n\n</original_code>\n"}], "temp": 0, "sample_size": 1, "logprobs": true, "model": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash"}, "response": {"samples": [{"content": "<translated_code>\nimport sys\n\nMOD = 1000000007\n\ndef mat_mul(A, B, mod):\n    n = len(A)\n    C = [[0] * n for _ in range(n)]\n    for i in range(n):\n        for k in range(n):\n            aik = A[i][k]\n            if aik:\n                for j in range(n):\n                    C[i][j] = (C[i][j] + aik * B[k][j]) % mod\n    return C\n\ndef mat_identity(n):\n    I = [[0] * n for _ in range(n)]\n    for i in range(n):\n        I[i][i] = 1\n    return I\n\ndef main():\n    data = sys.stdin.read().strip().split()\n    if not data:\n        return\n    n = int(data[0])\n    m = int(data[1])\n    size = m + 1\n\n    # bi is a 2D list of matrices, we will allocate as needed\n    # maximum x is such that m^x <= n, but we allocate up to 65 for safety\n    bi = [[None] * 65 for _ in range(65)]\n\n    # Initialize bi[0][0]\n    mat0 = [[0] * size for _ in range(size)]\n    for i in range(size):\n        mat0[i][i] = 1\n        mat0[0][i] = 1\n    bi[0][0] = mat0\n\n    # Compute x and y\n    y = 1\n    x = 0\n    while y * m <= n:\n        y *= m\n        x += 1\n\n    # Build matrices for t = 0..x\n    for t in range(0, x + 1):\n        if t > 0:\n            # bi[t][0] = bi[t-1][0] * product_{i=1}^{m-1} bi[t-1][i]\n            prod = [row[:] for row in bi[t-1][0]]\n            for i in range(1, m):\n                prod = mat_mul(prod, bi[t-1][i], MOD)\n            bi[t][0] = prod\n\n        # For i = 1..m-1\n        for i in range(1, m):\n            # copy bi[t][i-1]\n            mat = [row[:] for row in bi[t][i-1]]\n            # swap rows j and j+1 for j from m-2 down to 0\n            for j in range(m-2, -1, -1):\n                for k in range(size):\n                    mat[j][k], mat[j+1][k] = mat[j+1][k], mat[j][k]\n            # swap columns j and j+1 for j from m-2 down to 0\n            for j in range(m-2, -1, -1):\n                for k in range(size):\n                    mat[k][j], mat[k][j+1] = mat[k][j+1], mat[k][j]\n            bi[t][i] = mat\n\n    # Identity matrix I\n    I = mat_identity(size)\n\n    add = 0\n    z = 0\n    # Use the computed x and y from earlier\n    while add < n:\n        if add <= n - y:\n            add += y\n            I = mat_mul(I, bi[x][z], MOD)\n            z = (z + 1) % m\n        else:\n            y //= m\n            x -= 1\n\n    ans = 0\n    for i in range(size):\n        ans = (ans + I[i][m]) % MOD\n    print(ans)\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n0.95\n</confidence>", "token_logprobs": [-8.821448318485636e-06, 0.0, 0.0, -0.0005584587925113738, -0.047725409269332886, -0.0007107115816324949, -0.011055641807615757, -0.2700488269329071, -2.3841855067985307e-07, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -9.179073458653875e-06, 0.0, -1.1920928244535389e-07, 0.0, -3.6477376852417365e-05, -1.7762025890988298e-05, -0.0002768848498817533, -0.0004891153075732291, 0.0, -0.0015023384476080537, -3.6954811548639555e-06, 0.0, -0.023258375003933907, -0.00324758468195796, -0.04868781939148903, -3.576278118089249e-07, -0.08717093616724014, -3.576278118089249e-07, -1.0132738680113107e-05, 0.0, -4.5417706132866